WEBVTT

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.890
You can never return.

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.460
<i>It was a dream... right?</i>

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:39.710
What's wrong?

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:48.600
It seemed like a dream, but it was so vivid.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.820
But at the same time, 
it didn't seem like reality...

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.040
I was so scared.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:12.920
<b>Sakura's Clear Cards</b>

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.240
Was your dream today that scary?

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.610
At first, it felt like I was inside 
the book, and it was fun.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.470
In Alice's world?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:29.350
I was in Clock Land.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.610
I met Alice and all kinds 
of strange creatures,

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.110
and had some strange experiences...

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.870
Oh, right! There was a mirror!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.980
A mirror that could copy magic.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.040
But after that, the sound of 
the clock grew really loud,

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.490
and I heard something breaking, somewhere.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.270
Then I heard a voice.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.130
It said, "You can never return."

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:11.770
And throughout the dream, I thought 
Alice seemed very similar to me,

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:13.350
but today...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.660
Have you heard of "contrary dreams"?

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.960
It refers to dreams that are 
the opposite of reality.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:42.500
The opposite.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.800
If you had a scary dream, 
what would its opposite be?

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:50.350
Something fun would happen?

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:53.070
Precisely.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.480
Isn't it almost time for school?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.730
I'll go get my bag!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.990
I hope it was a contrary dream.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.920
But it could also be one that comes true.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.170
I won't let it.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.590
No matter what.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.970
You sure you're okay?

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.060
Maybe you should've stayed home from school.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.440
I'm fine.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:43.700
I can't tell my teacher I missed 
school because of a weird dream.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.570
<i>Dreams aren't what she needs to worry 
about, but I can't say that now.</i>

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.410
<i>The dream might have come from her magic...</i>

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.950
I don't think we should tell 
Sakura about this yet.

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:02.810
There must be a reason why Eriol didn't tell 
Sakura she's been makin' these cards.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:07.550
Since we can't contact him now, 
we can't learn what that reason was.

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.600
But would Eriol do anything 
that wouldn't help Sakura?

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.110
He would not.

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:13.910
Right.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.100
Also, everyone knew Eriol's 
house was torn down

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.690
and replaced with an amusement park.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.230
But the thing about that same house 
bein' put back together...

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:26.250
No one seemed to question that.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.360
And that magician?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.620
He hasn't tried doing 
anything to Sakura yet...

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:36.440
And man, Sakura and Akiho are 
such good buddies now.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.780
Do we really wanna make Sakura 
start suspecting her?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.380
For now, I shall keep it quiet.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.830
In return, do not leave our 
master, no matter what.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:53.600
<i>I won't leave her, but I can't 
exactly go into her dreams...</i>

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.850
<i>Besides, it might've been a premonition.</i>

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.690
Are you okay?

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:02.440
Huh?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.690
You seem down.

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.280
No, I'm great! Just great!

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.810
If anything, I might be a little hungry...

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:12.360
Even though you ate five 
rice balls for breakfast?

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:14.330
I'm a growin' boy!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:17.330
Dreams.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:19.620
We all know what a dream is.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:24.840
We also have bad dreams, 
and even waking dreams.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:28.220
These are similar to what 
we call "daydreams."

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.200
English also distinguishes

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.390
between dreams we have at night 
and dreams we strive for.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.960
Both are described as "dreams."

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.960
But the latter can also be 
expressed in another way.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:41.770
Miss Kinomoto.

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.010
Do you know what that is?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:49.870
Hope...

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:51.280
Exactly!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.110
Well done, Sakura-chan.

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.200
Huh?

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:00.750
Oh, I'm glad I got it right.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.760
Dreams?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.090
Yeah, they came up in our class.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:09.370
We talked about bad dreams 
and waking dreams, too!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:14.380
Oh, right. Not all dreams are good ones, huh?

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:17.510
And one word can have so 
many different meanings.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.260
Like "chau."

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.480
The word "chau" has several 
meanings, doesn't it?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.100
Huh?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.770
For example, in the Osaka 
dialect, they say...

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.970
"Chau, chau chau chaun chau?"

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.970
"No, that's not a chow chow, is it?"

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.990
Wait. Is that really "several meanings"?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:35.740
Sure, it is.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:39.990
The "chau" that means "no," 
and the "chow chow" dog breed?

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:40.950
Exactly.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:42.710
That's only two!

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.790
Two counts as several.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.250
You don't make sense! It was 
better when you flat-out lied!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.590
<i>That ain't the right intonation at all!</i>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.630
<i>It sounded nothin' like the Osaka dialect, 
and I'm itchin' to correct him!</i>

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.130
<i>Also, there are actually three "chaus"!</i>

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.760
Of course, words are all about 
how you interpret them.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.890
Some people interpret "chau" as "no,"

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.060
and others would think it's the dog.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:09.770
A word might be a nickname for someone,

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.860
or it might be part of some regional dialect.

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:16.450
So I hope people will interpret words in the 
way that brings the most happiness.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:18.940
Yamazaki-kun...

00:09:21.970 --> 00:09:23.460
You're right.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.910
Sorry I'm late again!

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:35.180
It's okay. We went ahead and ate.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.970
Done with everything?

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:40.470
Oh, no... My call didn't go through.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.760
Maybe it was a bad time for them.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.390
Or maybe the signal was too weak.

00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.150
<i>His communications are bein' blocked, too...</i>

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.690
I'll try again from home, later.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.910
Sorry to make you worry.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:00.410
One, two, three, four.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.280
One, two, three, four.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.280
One, two, three, four.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:05.620
One, two—

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.460
Mihara-san, a little more to your left!

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.300
Okay.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.790
Kinomoto-san, you're a bit behind.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.780
Be careful after you turn around.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.050
Okay!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.920
One, two, three, four.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.130
One, two, three, four.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.180
Okay, break time!

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:25.050
The Cheerleading Club is 
practicing hard, too!

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:28.520
I'm sorry! We're supposed to 
be practicing ourselves!

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.070
The others aren't even here yet.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.030
This might be rude of me to say,

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.200
but Sakura-san and I...

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.700
You're very similar to each other.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:51.290
And that's not rude at all.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.630
It would make Sakura-chan very happy!

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.100
You really think so?

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:59.620
Does it bother you?

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.130
It makes me very, very happy!

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:10.960
But when I think that I might be doing 
something to bother Sakura-san...

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.510
Did something happen?

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.310
I have these dreams.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:21.940
Remember the book I showed you, 
<i>Alice in Clock Land</i>?

00:11:22.690 --> 00:11:24.270
I have dreams about that book.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:29.790
The dreams follow the book's story, 
and it progresses a little, each time.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:33.290
Lots of different things 
happen to Alice, but...

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.000
In the one I had today,

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.940
something scary caught her, and...

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.220
And in this dream, Alice...

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:52.190
looked like Sakura-san.

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.810
You can never return.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:03.330
What's wrong, Sakura-chan?

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:04.900
Huh?

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.970
Oh... Nothing.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.180
I'm done with the bath!

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.500
Okay!

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.600
Toya-kun, go ahead and take yours.

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.400
Sure.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:32.240
This is the last one.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.160
Hamburg steaks for tomorrow?

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:39.770
I thought I'd put some in tomorrow's 
lunches and freeze the rest.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:41.960
I can't wait!

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:49.120
What?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.450
Go to bed, right now.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.040
Don't do anything else.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:58.720
Ugh!

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.560
It's supposed to get chilly 
tonight, so keep warm.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:03.770
Okay.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.770
<b>Eriol Hiiragizawa</b>

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.770
I still can't get through...

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:21.820
His magic can do even that?

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:26.900
Even if it can...

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.840
I will protect her!

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.930
You should've joined me in 
the bath, Kero-chan...

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.340
Have a seat! I'll dry your hair!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:46.710
That's funny... I'm sure I gave you the 
same amount of snacks as usual.

00:13:46.710 --> 00:13:49.970
Stop talkin' like I only do stuff 
when ya give me food!

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.470
Thanks.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.010
Hey, Kero-chan.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:57.850
Yeah?

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:02.240
The first time I talked to 
you in our basement...

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:06.690
At first, I didn't understand why 
a stuffed animal was talking.

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:09.360
Then I was suddenly a Cardcaptor...

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:14.070
Later, Mizuki-sensei came along,

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:17.210
and I found out about Yukito-san and Yue-san.

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:21.110
Then Eriol-kun and the others came, 
and a lot happened, but...

00:14:29.170 --> 00:14:34.460
I'm really glad I met all of them.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:36.970
Sakura?

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:41.190
There are still lots of things 
I don't understand,

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:45.410
and I'm always worrying people 
or causing trouble.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:48.870
Not everything that happens is fun,

00:14:48.870 --> 00:14:51.480
but even if I'm facing something stressful,

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:55.850
everyone is here for me, so I—

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:02.670
Sakura?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:16.660
Sakura!

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.770
You okay?

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:22.300
Yeah.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:24.010
Sakura?

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:32.490
Who the heck is that?

00:15:36.550 --> 00:15:38.460
It's the one I saw in my dream.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.500
Is this a dream?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.830
No, it ain't no dream!

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.580
<i>Release!</i>

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:51.980
<i>Flight!</i>

00:15:58.670 --> 00:15:59.850
You're scared?

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.410
I'm sorry. Will you fly with me?

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.060
Thank you.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:07.950
Let's go, Kero-chan!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:09.090
Right!

00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.600
What the heck?!

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.100
It's no use. My magic's bein' blocked.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:27.640
Kero-chan...

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:38.350
We've met in my dreams, right?

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:42.320
Is there something you want to tell me?

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:44.210
Something you want me to do?

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.590
Tell me.

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.140
Are you...

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:01.500
Sakura!

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.790
Kero-chan!

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:05.950
I'm okay!

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:15.200
Get outta there!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.060
<i>Blaze!</i>

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.010
<i>Aqua!</i>

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.160
<i>Spiral!</i>

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.300
No!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.460
No... Don't go over there!

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.560
<i>Release!</i>

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:50.830
<i>Release!</i>

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:00.770
Flight-san!

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.230
<i>Akiho-chan?</i>

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:36.720
You used the time magic again.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.560
It was an emergency.

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:54.250
How is Akiho-san?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.910
Dreaming, just like always.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:01.370
Put simply, she's acting in her sleep.

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:02.310
Will she remember?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:06.590
Even if she does, it will be as 
something in her dream.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:09.320
But Sakura-san...

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.680
She'll probably remember it.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.130
Then, I have no choice.

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:21.060
Wait. You're really going to do this?

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:24.750
These cards aren't enough...

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:30.040
to activate that magic.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.620
<i>Tina Rie Triax.</i>

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:48.520
<i>Time, in accordance with 
the covenant, turn back.</i>

00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:14.690
Huh?

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:32.240
Even for you, turning back 
time that far is insane.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:37.060
Even so...

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.360
You're still doing it.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:45.530
Even you have stayed here, 
so you can see the activation

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:47.880
of the taboo magic, have you not?

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:50.360
Well, that's one reason.

00:21:52.760 --> 00:21:54.260
The other is...

00:21:59.070 --> 00:21:59.910
And?

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:00.680
Huh?

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:03.030
"Everyone is here for me, so I..."

00:22:03.030 --> 00:22:05.000
You weren't done talkin' yet, right?

00:22:11.610 --> 00:22:12.420
Sakura?

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:18.510
So I'm not alone.

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.790
I'm sure I'll be all right.

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:29.180
Atta girl! I knew you'd make 
a great Cardcaptor Sakura!

00:24:04.130 --> 00:24:05.200
Take care.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:06.470
I will!

00:24:15.390 --> 00:24:17.040
Syaoran-kun!

00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:27.240
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:26.610 --> 00:24:27.860
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:36.740
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:27.860 --> 00:24:36.740
<b>K</b>

00:24:28.030 --> 00:24:29.470
Time flies like an arrow!

00:24:29.470 --> 00:24:32.330
This marks the final episode of 
<i>Cardcaptor Sakura: Clear Card</i>,

00:24:32.330 --> 00:24:35.800
which means this segment's end, 
too. Last up, I'm introducin'...

00:24:35.800 --> 00:24:36.980
Me!

00:24:36.980 --> 00:24:40.160
A golden body and white wings, 
and isn't that smooth hip line sexy?

00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:43.620
The rapid-fire talks I give are so 
cool, they're loved by all ages!

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:43.250
<b>You're just a noisy
 yellow dumpling</b>

00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:46.000
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:46.000
<b>K</b>

00:24:43.620 --> 00:24:47.430
And next time, my new segment, 
<i>Kero-chan's Eat Till You Drop</i>, begins...

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:47.000
<b>That show doesn't exist 
(for the second time)</b>

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.250
<b>Kero-chan's 
Eat Till 
You Drop</b>

00:24:47.000 --> 00:24:48.250
<b>Yum!</b>

00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:50.560
I'll eat tasty world foods, and show 
how amazing and cool I am.

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:50.010
<b>To be precise,
the idea was scrapped</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:52.930
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:52.930
<b>K</b>

00:24:50.560 --> 00:24:55.020
Anyway, thanks for watchin'! I look 
forward to seein' y'all again!

00:24:54.010 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Ta-ta</b>

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
